 more  motivation  and it's also just it doesn't make sense  to have a one  narrow long term goal that you're  looking at without trying to figure out  in between  what are those things that are going to  help me to achieve more  happiness more stability whatever it is  right now  and those short-term goals are going to  be very important for that  so for me for example my short-term goal  is to finish there's a curriculum that i  can do for free at stanford on grants  management because i work so closely  with faculty who have to apply for  grants i want to understand what they're  going through  and then finally i know people say this  all the time but i i especially right  now in this environment of  not always being as connected my last  my last tip is really to seek mentorship  you want to head to that last slide  connect with those who have careers you  admire or achievements you admire don't  just say okay well this person also has  an mba so i'm just going to ask them  are they in a position that you want to  be in are they  kind of at a at a place in their career  where they seem to be happy they seem to  be thriving and it's something you want  to be able to  um replicate in your own  it's so important to get insight from  people who have been there and  especially for people who are from  underserved  or under resourced backgrounds if you  can connect with someone who  not has the exact same life experience  but who's also had to  go through things that maybe the  majority groups have not had to  that can also really help to be able to  see  there is a way forward there are going  to be hurdles it is going to be hard but  so and so did it this is how they did it  i can do it too  um i am very very very lucky to have  several people in my  past that have been excellent mentors  sometimes they've also been my managers  i know that's very rarely the case  but it's it's just so important to  really understand  how having someone who isn't  responsible for you